Short:        Modern TCP/IP stack with IPv6 and prefs
Author:       farsonic@gmail.com (farsonic and the Riptide developers)
Uploader:     farsonic@gmail.com (farsonic)
Type:         comm/tcp
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0
Requires:     68020 or better, 2 MB RAM, a SANA-II network driver (or an
              emulator's uaenet.device); util/libs/mui38usr.lha is
              optional (the MUI preferences editor; GadTools otherwise)
Distribution: Aminet
Kurz:         Moderner TCP/IP-Stack mit IPv6 und Prefs

Riptide is a free TCP/IP stack for AmigaOS 3.x on the 68020 to 68060.
It replaces AmiTCP, Miami or Roadshow: existing network programs run
unchanged, and the stack itself is built like a current one.

Features
--------
* bsdsocket.library 4 with the AmiTCP API plus the Roadshow and Miami
  extension calls, riptide.library and usergroup.library
* TCP after the Linux stack: CUBIC with HyStart++, SACK, RACK-TLP, PRR,
  F-RTO, ECN, TCP Fast Open, path MTU black hole detection, Happy
  Eyeballs v2, LEDBAT background transfers, buffer auto-tuning
* IPv4 and IPv6: DHCP, SLAAC, link-local addresses, several network
  cards, VLANs (802.1Q), multicast (IGMPv3/MLDv2), mDNS, NTP, QoS
* DNS resolver with EDNS0, DNS over TCP and negative caching
* any SANA-II device (Ethernet or point-to-point) and MNI drivers,
  with DMA copy hooks for drivers that have them
* Linux-style tools: ip, ifconfig, route, arp, netstat, ping,
  traceroute, host, sysctl, hostname, nc, an ftp client, speedtest and
  rtdiag (collects everything for a bug report)
* RiptidePrefs: a MUI preferences editor (GadTools without MUI) for
  every setting, with a live status page: throughput graphs,
  connections, routes, counters
* stackprobe: tests every bsdsocket feature on any stack, to compare
  stacks (Riptide: 208 passed, 0 failed)
* hand-written 680x0 checksum and copy routines; one binary for the
  68020 to 68060
* a developer SDK (bsdsocket.library and riptide.library FD files,
  protos, inlines, pragmas) in the SDK drawer

Installing
----------
Double-click Install_Riptide (the standard Amiga Installer). It copies
the programs to C:, writes ENVARC:Riptide/riptide.conf for your network
card (DHCP or a static address) and adds Riptide to S:User-Startup; run
it again to update or uninstall. The manual is Riptide/Docs/AMIGA.md.

Under FS-UAE or WinUAE use uaenet.device (uae_sana2 = 1,
network_card = a2065) and turn the emulator's bsdsocket.library
emulation off.

